L["TUTORIAL_WELCOME_TITLE"] = "A starting point for your route"
L["TUTORIAL_WELCOME_BODY"] = "APR Recorder helps you build routes for Azeroth Pilot Reloaded: record your journey, edit the steps, then save and test in APR.\n\nIt is not a magic tool: not everything is automatic. Some actions must be added manually. You may need to reorder steps, merge their contents or split them into several steps. Always review and test a recording.\n\nStart the tour to see pointers on the workshop controls, or Skip to explore on your own. You can restart it from Tools. The tour does not start recording or change your route."
L["TUTORIAL_RECORD_TITLE"] = "Create a route and record"
L["TUTORIAL_RECORD_BODY"] = "Create a route with New route, or select an existing one above, then use this button to start or stop recording.\n\nSupported events capture quests, objectives, flights and some interactions. Check the recording status: browsing another route does not change the recording target."
L["TUTORIAL_STEPS_TITLE"] = "Find and edit your steps"
L["TUTORIAL_STEPS_BODY"] = "Search, filter and select a step in this list to edit it. Add inserts a step of your chosen type.\n\nFollow recording and Jump to latest help you inspect new captures. Follow pauses while the draft has unsaved changes. Compact mode switches between the list and inspector."
L["TUTORIAL_REWORK_TITLE"] = "Reorder, merge and split manually"
L["TUTORIAL_REWORK_BODY"] = "Move steps with the arrows or Move to step. Duplicate and Delete help restructure the route.\n\nTo merge: copy the useful fields into one step, check them, then remove the redundant step. To split: duplicate a step and keep only the appropriate fields in each copy. These adjustments are manual. Save a copy before major changes."
L["TUTORIAL_FIELDS_TITLE"] = "Describe what the player must do"
L["TUTORIAL_FIELDS_BODY"] = "Edit the selected step here: objectives, coordinates, actions, instructions and conditions. Add or remove fields as needed.\n\nThe search icon opens the associated selector for IDs or translation keys, including Note. ID lists add the selected value; the text format replaces the value. Create a route and add a step to try it."
L["TUTORIAL_COMMANDS_TITLE"] = "Use the command catalog"
L["TUTORIAL_COMMANDS_BODY"] = "Search or filter available commands and mark favorites. Commands may open an input or selection window.\n\nThey act on the recording route, usually its last step, not the step selected in the draft. Use the inspector for earlier steps. /aprrc help lists the commands."
L["TUTORIAL_BAR_TITLE"] = "Customize the command bar"
L["TUTORIAL_BAR_BODY"] = "Drag commands between the catalog and bar columns to add, remove or reorder shortcuts.\n\nBar settings controls visibility, orientation, size, backgrounds and anchoring to the workshop. The bar appears while recording. Drag an icon to move it; page arrows appear when needed. Reset restores the defaults."
L["TUTORIAL_ROUTE_TITLE"] = "Configure the route and protect your edits"
L["TUTORIAL_ROUTE_BODY"] = "Save commits the current draft. Save a copy preserves it as another route; Reload discards it. Undo and Redo help correct edits. Drafts survive closing the workshop.\n\nIf recording changed the route in the background, hold Shift, Ctrl or Alt while clicking Save to replace it with exactly this draft, without merging those automatic changes. This keeps the content of a copy under the current route name."
L["TUTORIAL_LUA_TITLE"] = "Edit or copy Lua data"
L["TUTORIAL_LUA_BODY"] = "Use the Lua editor for advanced edits or pasting compatible route data. Ctrl+A / Ctrl+C copies it; Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y undoes or redoes.\n\nInvalid Lua must be corrected before returning to visual editing. The Route tab provides route metadata and conditions. Use the Parallel steps tab to manage parallel groups, their conditions and steps. Save a copy before extensive edits."
L["TUTORIAL_TOOLS_TITLE"] = "Coordinates, IDs and other tools"
L["TUTORIAL_TOOLS_BODY"] = "Restart the tour with this button. Tools also provides coordinates, extra text export, command references and settings.\n\nSettings controls quest IDs, fonts, the minimap icon, campaign flags and profiles. Left-click the minimap icon to open the workshop; right-click to toggle the addon."
L["TUTORIAL_EXPORT_TITLE"] = "Save, import and test in APR"
L["TUTORIAL_EXPORT_BODY"] = "Saved routes are automatically synchronized with APR, including during recording. Draft edits are published when you click Save. Select the copy in APR's Custom tab and test its steps, objectives, coordinates and conditions.\n\nUse Import from APR to create an editable copy of an APR route. The original route stays unchanged. You can search by name or route key."

L["SAVE_OVERRIDE_HELP"] = "Hold Shift, Ctrl or Alt while clicking Save to replace the saved route with exactly the current draft, including your Lua edits. Automatic changes made in the background are overwritten, not merged. This saves the same content as Save a copy, but keeps the current route name."
L["SAVE_CONFLICT_HELP"] = "The saved route changed. Save a copy to keep your edits, reload the saved route, or hold Shift, Ctrl or Alt while clicking Save to overwrite it with the current draft."

L["TUTORIAL_START"] = "Start the tour"

